TITLE:: RERenderedPlayer
summary:: A take rendered offline played live: its WAV into the chain, its visuals tape to the page
categories:: Libraries>reCording
related:: Guides/reCording, Classes/REScorePlayer, Classes/REScoreEditor, Classes/REReplay, Classes/REVisualsTape, Classes/REOfflineTap

DESCRIPTION::
An link::Classes/REScorePlayer:: for a take that HomewareSC's code::scripts/take.sh render <take> --viz:: rendered: at the take's aligned start on the song's clock it plays the render's WAV (the undecoded field, summed into the song's chain and decoded live as the instruments are) and sends the visuals tape (code::<take>/<take>.viz.json::, link::Classes/REVisualsTape::) to HomewareVisuals through link::Classes/RCVisuals::, next to the takes the program plays live. Nothing is fired (the render made the sound) but the take's tempo events; every event is still reported through code::onEvent:: (the score page's played marks, link::Classes/REScoreVisuals::) and the head runs. The sidecar next to the take, code::<take>.render.json:: (link::Classes/REScore#*readRender::), names the WAV, its convention, the latency, the start and the tape; the WAV and the tape are in the render's folder, code::<take>/:: next to the take. link::Classes/REScoreEditor#-play:: makes one when a take has a render (the lanes page's Play).

A section the live server cannot play whole (the LSystem's dense growths) is thus recorded as a take (the audio may break up: the take holds the lines and the inputs), rendered offline with its visuals, and played back as one piece of the set.

subsection:: Timing
WAV time 0 is the take's start on the render's clock. The render bundled its sounds with its latency λr, the live server plays with its own λl: the WAV is cued λr in and its synth sent in a latency bundle at the start beat (seconds S0), so WAV time code::w:: sounds at code::S0 + w - λr + λl::, and a tape message at code::t:: goes out at code::S0 + t - λr + λl::, the same offset: the messages sent when a sound starts (notes, births, cycles, lines) land with their sound whatever the two latencies; a message a rig sends without latency (gone, clear, hair) is off by code::λl - λr::, nothing with the one server-options file. The WAV cannot stretch, so the head follows it (link::Classes/REScorePlayer#-tempoMode::): code::\clock:: (the default) starts at the aligned beat of the song's clock and goes on on a clock of its own at the take's tempo, the same beat at the same second (link::#-ownClock::): the head, the played marks and the take's tempo events follow the WAV whatever the song's tempo, which is left alone (the render is then off the song's grid, said); code::\take:: sets the song's clock to the take's tempo and the head stays on it. An own clock is stopped at the end and kept a few seconds after (SuperCollider 3.14.1's code::TempoClock.stop:: ends the clock after the evaluation: dropped before, it is collected under its thread). The tape is played from the take's code::from:: (link::Classes/REVisualsTape#-play::), and with link::#-fxCue:: the effects page is cued with those seconds as they sound.

subsection:: Routing
A raw render (code::hoa acn-n3d::, the chain's channels) is summed into the chain's signal stage (the head of its group) and decoded live as the instruments are, at the gig and at home alike; an AmbiX render (code::acn-sn3d::, the chain's own decoded output) or a stereo one goes onto the chain's output bus after the decoder (an AmbiX one only when the live chain decodes to code::\ambix::: render with code::--decode raw:: otherwise). The chain's buses and groups are looked up at play: a scene init rebuilds them.

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: new
argument:: score
argument:: song
argument:: render
The sidecar as a dictionary (link::Classes/REScore#*readRender::) or its path.

METHOD:: fromTake
The take at path with the render next to it; nil (an error logged) without one.
argument:: path
argument:: song

INSTANCEMETHODS::

METHOD:: play
As the parent's, after the WAV is cued: refused without a running server or a WAV; code::loop:: is warned about and ignored; a latency other than the render's is warned about; with code::\clock::, a song's clock not at the take's tempo is said (the render is off its grid).
argument:: quant
argument:: from
The take's beat to start from: the WAV is cued there.
argument:: to
argument:: loop
argument:: atBeat

METHOD:: stop
The events, the WAV and the tape.
METHOD:: free
Stops and drops the cue buffer.
METHOD:: fire
True for every event (reported, not acted on) but a code::tempo:: event, fired, and one marked code::replay: false::.

METHOD:: routing
code::\auto:: (the default: by the render's convention and the chain's decoder), code::\signal::, code::\out::.
METHOD:: route
The route chosen at play.
METHOD:: render
METHOD:: replay
The link::Classes/REReplay:: playing the WAV.
METHOD:: tape
The link::Classes/REVisualsTape::, read at play.
METHOD:: tapeClock
The clock the tape plays on (SystemClock).
METHOD:: latency
The render's.
METHOD:: wav
METHOD:: duration
The render's seconds (the take and its tail).
METHOD:: ownClock
With code::tempoMode \clock::, while it plays: the head's clock at the take's tempo, from the start; nil otherwise.

METHOD:: mediaSecs
The seconds WAV time 0 corresponds to, once playing.

METHOD:: onStart
code::{ |player, mediaSecs, fromSecs| }::, called in the Routine at the start, the WAV and the tape started.

METHOD:: fxCue
true (the default): code::'/fx/start' <fromSecs>:: is sent through link::Classes/RCVisuals:: as the WAV's code::from:: sounds (HomewareVisuals' effects page cues its muted video to it: a session over a rendered take, link::Guides/reCording#Reprocessing::), and code::'/fx/stop':: at stop and at the end. Harmless without the page.

EXAMPLES::

code::
// rendered: scripts/take.sh render "<piece>/Scores/<take>.json" --viz
~p = RERenderedPlayer.fromTake(~rec.lastPath, ~song);
~viz.attachPlayer(~p);     // the score page follows
~p.play([4, 0]);           // on the next bar, as a live replay would
~p.stop;
~p.free;

// next to a take the program plays live
~q = REScorePlayer(REScore.read(otherTake), ~song); ~q.play([4, 0]);
::
